Article 9
(1) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point at each SKPD in the Region consists of officials and/or staff whose field covers planning and/or program duties.
(2) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the duties to:
a. promote Gender Mainstreaming in the work unit;
b. facilitate the preparation of work plans and budgeting of SKPD that are Gender Responsive;
c. implement training, socialization, advocacy of Gender Mainstreaming to all officials and staff within the SKPD environment;
d. report the implementation of PUG to the leadership of SKPD;
e. encourage the implementation of Gender Analysis on policies, programs, and activities in the work unit; and
f. facilitate the preparation of gender data at each SKPD.
(3) The Gender Mainstreaming Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and determined by the head/leader of SKPD.

CHAPTER V
CHILD-FRIENDLY REGENCY
Article 31
(1) To realize the Fulfillment of Children's Rights, it shall be implemented in an integrated and systematic manner from all sectors on a sustainable basis through the Policy for Development of CFR.
(2) The Policy for Development of CFR as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be directed toward the fulfillment of children's rights, comprising:
a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and e. special protection.
(3) The Stages of Development of CFR as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be further regulated in a Regent Regulation.

