7.1.text:
Article 10
(1) Regional Government submits reports on PUG implementation to the Provincial Government periodically every 6 (six) months.
(2) Reports on PUG implementation as referred to in paragraph (1), include: a. implementation of programs and activities;
b. agencies involved in the implementation of activities;
c. activity targets;
d. budget utilization sourced from APBD or other sources; e. problems encountered; and
f. efforts that have been undertaken.
(3) Procedures for reporting PUG implementation in the region shall be further regulated in a Regent Regulation.

Article 19
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of Regional Government as referred to in Article 18 letter a, include:
a. implementing policies for the protection of women and children established by the government;
b. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women and children in the Region;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity; and
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government establishes programs and activities for the protection of women and children in the Regional Action Plan as a basis for the Regional Government in implementing protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be established by Regent Regulation.

Article 14
Regional Government implements policies, programs, and activities of PKHP in various development sectors, through:
a. coordination of implementation of policies, programs, and activities of PKHP among SKPD;
b. cooperation with other Regional Governments in the implementation of policies, programs, and activities of PKHP;
c. strengthening of institutional capacity of PUG for the implementation of PKHP; d. facilitation of PKHP services;
e. provision of PKHP services;
f. implementation of PKHP affirmative action; and
g. preparation of PKHP data collection system.

